§ `Order 18, Division 3 -- Appeal from District Judge and Magistrate to General Division (rules 17 to 23)`

§§ `Rule 17 -- bringing of appeal`

-- src:1858 | 17. —(1) A party who intends to appeal to the General Division against the decision of a District Judge or Magistrate hearing any application at first instance, or hearing the merits of an originating application, or against the decision of a District Judge hearing any appeal, must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35 — ( a )
-- src:1859 | within 14 days after the date of the District Judge’s or Magistrate’s decision; or
-- src:1860 | ( b )
-- src:1861 | in a case where a request for further arguments has been made under Rule 18, within 14 days after — (i)
-- src:1862 | the District Judge or Magistrate affirms, varies or sets aside the decision after hearing further arguments; or
-- src:1863 | (ii)
-- src:1864 | the parties are informed, or it is deemed, that the District Judge or Magistrate does not require further arguments. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref O 18 r 17(1) (src:1858-1864)
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under Rule 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the District Judge's or Magistrate's decision` IS A DATE
      `the date the District Judge or Magistrate affirms, varies or sets aside the decision after hearing further arguments` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the parties are informed, or it is deemed, that the District Judge or Magistrate does not require further arguments` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 18 r 17(1) the date after which the 14 days for the notice of appeal run` MEANS
    IF `a request for further arguments has been made under Rule 18`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the District Judge or Magistrate affirms, varies or sets aside the decision after hearing further arguments`
        WHEN JUST affirmed THEN JUST affirmed
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the parties are informed, or it is deemed, that the District Judge or Magistrate does not require further arguments`
    ELSE JUST `the date of the District Judge's or Magistrate's decision` -- limb (a); when a request was made the encoding takes limb (b): fork 18.2

@ref O 18 r 17(1) (src:1858-1864)
`o 18 r 17(1) the period for the notice of appeal` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 18 r 17(1) (src:1858-1864)
GIVEN `the party intends to appeal against a decision of a District Judge or Magistrate or against a decision of a District Judge hearing an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 17(1) the notice of appeal in Form 35 is filed and served in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the party intends to appeal against a decision of a District Judge or Magistrate or against a decision of a District Judge hearing an appeal`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party who intends to appeal to the General Division against the decision of a District Judge or Magistrate"
        IF `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` AND (`the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
