§§ `Rule 19 -- permission to appeal`

-- src:1875 | 19. —(1) Where permission to appeal is required, a party must apply to the District Judge or Magistrate for such permission and serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the District Judge’s or Magistrate’s decision. (2) Where the District Judge or Magistrate does not grant permission to appeal, the party may apply to the General Division for such permission and must serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the District Judge’s or Magistrate’s decision not to grant permission.
@ref O 18 r 19(1) (src:1875)
`o 18 r 19(1) the period after the date of the decision for applying for permission` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 18 r 19(1) (src:1875)
