      `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application was made and served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 19(1) the application for permission to the District Judge or Magistrate is made and served in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `permission to appeal is required`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where permission to appeal is required" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` AND (`the date the application was made and served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of the District Judge’s or Magistrate’s decision" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
@ref O 18 r 19(2) (src:1875)
