    WHEN JUST required THEN IF amount EQUALS required THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must provide security in the following amounts"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
@ref O 18 r 20(5) (src:1887-1890)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 20(5) kind of action appealed from`
      `the number of sets of respondents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 18 r 20(3) and (5) the total security the appellant must provide` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 18 r 20(5) the amount of security required` kind
    WHEN JUST required THEN JUST (required TIMES `the number of sets of respondents`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

