-- src:1911 | (5) The parties to the appeal must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal written submissions (including any bundle of authorities) on why the District Judge’s or Magistrate’s decision is to be upheld, set aside or varied in accordance with the following timelines: ( a )
-- src:1912 | where the District Judge or Magistrate certifies under paragraph (2)( a ) that he or she has already issued a written judgment or grounds of decision, within 14 days after the Registry notifies of such certification by the District Judge or Magistrate;
-- src:1913 | ( b )
-- src:1914 | where the District Judge or Magistrate certifies under paragraph (2)( b ) that he or she intends to issue written grounds of decision, within 14 days after the Registry notifies that a copy of the written grounds of decision is ready for collection;
-- src:1915 | ( c )
-- src:1916 | where the District Judge or Magistrate certifies under paragraph (2)( c ) that the certified transcript of the official record of hearing sets out his or her grounds of decision sufficiently, within 14 days after the Registry notifies of such certification by the District Judge or Magistrate;
-- src:1917 | ( d )
-- src:1918 | where it is presumed under paragraph (2) that no further written grounds of decision will be issued, within 28 days after the filing and service of the notice of appeal;
-- src:1919 | ( e )
-- src:1920 | where the appellant or the respondent has applied in writing to proceed with the appeal under paragraph (3)( b ), within 14 days after the Registrar notifies that the appeal is to proceed. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 18 r 21(5) (src:1911-1920)
GIVEN trigger IS A `o 18 r 21(5) what starts the period for the written submissions`
GIVETH A Period
`o 18 r 21(5) the period for the written submissions` MEANS
    CONSIDER trigger
    WHEN `o 18 r 21(5)(a) the notification of the certificate that a written judgment or grounds of decision were already issued` THEN `o 18 r 21(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 21(5)(b) the notification that a copy of the written grounds of decision is ready for collection` THEN `o 18 r 21(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 21(5)(c) the notification of the certificate that the certified transcript sets out the grounds of decision sufficiently` THEN `o 18 r 21(5)(a) the period after the notification`
    WHEN `o 18 r 21(5)(d) the presumption that no further written grounds of decision will be issued` THEN `o 18 r 21(5)(d) the period after the filing and service of the notice of appeal`
    WHEN `o 18 r 21(5)(e) the notification that the appeal is to proceed after an application to proceed` THEN `o 18 r 21(5)(a) the period after the notification`

@ref O 18 r 21(5)(a) (src:1912)
`o 18 r 21(5)(a) the period after the notification` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
